export function Privacy() {
  const {company}=useSiteContent();
  return <><PageHero current="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="YOUR INFORMATION" title="Privacy & enquiry information." description="How information submitted through this website is used to handle your business enquiry."/><section className="section"><div className="container legal-content"><p className="small-note">Website privacy notice · Haviss 3D Metrology Solutions</p><h2>Information you choose to provide</h2><p>When you contact Haviss, you may provide your name, company, email address, phone number, location, equipment details and a description of your requirement. If you upload a file, the enquiry includes that attachment. Please share only information needed for the enquiry and only files you are authorized to provide.</p><h2>How enquiry information is used</h2><p>Information is used to review your requirement, contact you about the enquiry, prepare a proposed scope and maintain the related business record. An enquiry is not consent to unrelated marketing.</p><h2>Storage and authorized access</h2><p>Where online submission is enabled, enquiry records and attachments are held through the website’s configured database and storage services. Access to enquiry records and private attachments is restricted to authorized staff. Service providers supporting hosting, data storage, security and email delivery may process information for these purposes.</p><h2>Security and retention</h2><p>Access controls and upload restrictions help protect submitted information. No internet service can guarantee absolute security. Information should be retained only for the enquiry, related business requirements and any applicable record-keeping obligations. Contact Haviss to discuss the handling or removal of your information.</p><h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2><p>Staff authentication uses browser storage to maintain an authenticated session. The website does not include advertising trackers by default. When enabled, the anti-spam service may process technical information to help identify automated submissions.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Links to maps, email applications and other services take you to providers with their own privacy practices. Review those providers’ notices when using their services.</p><h2>Contact and requests</h2><p>For questions about an enquiry record, corrections or deletion requests, {company.email&&<>email <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> or </>}call <a href={company.phoneHref}>{company.phone}</a>. We may need to confirm your identity before acting on a request.</p><address>{company.name}<br/>{company.registeredOffice}</address></div></section></>;
}

